            <ArticleTitle>A rare case of uterine adenomyosis in a Siamese cat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>709-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old, female Siamese cat with a long-term history of megestrol acetate treatment for suppression of estrus was presented with vomiting and abdominal pain. Uterine adenomyosis was diagnosed after an ovariohysterectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
